Oddly enough, no. Not unless you're trying to write spellbooks, but no
scrolls. If you're writing scrolls, your MM is going to have fewer than
25 charges when it starts getting dry. An uncursed ?oC will add at most
14 charges, and then bring it up to 50. A blessed ?oC will add at most
25 charges, and then also bring it up to 50.
The only difference occurs if your marker is well over 25 charges when
you read the scroll. A blessed ?oC _may_ then raise the total to over
50, in which case it will end up having 75. An uncursed scroll won't do
that. But this will only occur if the thing you're trying to write needs
more than 25 charges; this might occur with the ?oGeno, but it's not
very likely, and all other scrolls need less.

